<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 19 July, from 484 to 1979.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/antioch-on-the-orontes" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antioch-on-the-orontes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">484 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,542 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The rebel general Leontius is crowned emperor at Tarsus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Leontius, a general of the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>, was crowned emperor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarsus">Tarsus</a> in a rebellion against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeno-emperor">Emperor Zeno</a> that lasted until 488. He was recognised in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> and made it his capital.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch-on-the-orontes">Antioch</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/711">711 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,315 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tariq ibn Ziyad defeats King Roderic at Guadalete</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Umayyad forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tariq-ibn-ziyad">Tariq ibn Ziyad</a> defeated and killed the Visigothic king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roderic">Roderic</a>, by the traditional date. Within a few years most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> was under Muslim rule, the beginning of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tariq-ibn-ziyad">Tariq ibn Ziyad</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">998 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,028 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A Fatimid army defeats the Byzantines at the Battle of Apamea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Byzantine forces under Damian Dalassenos, besieging Apamea, were winning against a Fatimid relief army until a lone Kurdish rider killed Dalassenos and their army fled in panic. The defeat forced Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a> to campaign there in person the next year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arab-byzantine-wars">Arab–Byzantine wars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1333">1333 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">693 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The English defeat the Scots at Halidon Hill</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Outside besieged Berwick, Edward III and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-balliol">Edward Balliol</a> defeated a Scottish army under the regent Archibald Douglas that was trying to relieve the town. Douglas was killed, and the defeat forced the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> II into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-halidon-hill">Battle of Halidon Hill</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-war-of-scottish-independence">Second War of Scottish Independence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1553">1553 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">473 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mary Tudor is proclaimed Queen of England in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">As support for Lady Jane Grey collapsed, the Privy Council proclaimed Mary queen to cheering crowds. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>'s first undisputed queen regnant restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> and burned some 280 Protestants.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1848">1848 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Seneca Falls Convention opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-cady-stanton">Elizabeth Cady Stanton</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucretia">Lucretia</a> Mott opened the first women's rights convention in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. Its Declaration of Sentiments, stating that 'all men and women are created equal', launched the suffrage movement.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1870">1870 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">156 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">France declares war on Prussia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Provoked by Bismarck's edited Ems Dispatch, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a>'s government declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>. Within months <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> was defeated, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">Second Empire</a> fell and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> was proclaimed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-prussia">Kingdom of Prussia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1979">1979 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">47 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sandinista rebels take power in Nicaragua</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two days after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anastasio-somoza-debayle">Anastasio Somoza Debayle</a> fled, Sandinista forces entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/managua">Managua</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somoza-family">Somoza family</a>'s 43-year rule. The revolution soon drew the US into backing the Contra insurgency.</p></div></li></ol>
